<BaseLayout title="About — Vitor Sacramento" description="Professional focus and working principles of Vitor Sacramento.">
  <div class="shell"><header class="page-head"><p class="eyebrow">About</p><h1>Engineering with spatial and environmental context.</h1><p class="lead">A cross-disciplinary practice spanning data engineering, geospatial analysis, applied AI and software systems.</p></header><article class="prose section"><h2>Approach</h2><p>I focus on turning complex data into systems that are understandable, testable and useful. Spatial context, data quality and operational constraints are part of the design—not an afterthought.</p><h2>Current portfolio status</h2><p>This site is being assembled from a structured audit of public and private repositories. Only work with verified ownership, evidence and publication approval will appear as a case study.</p><h2>Principles</h2><p>Prefer reproducible pipelines, explicit limitations, careful handling of sensitive data and documentation that describes the software as it actually exists.</p></article></div>
